ck, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back instead to v2.2.9 (last healthy production release before v2.3.0) in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollout reported VERIFIED. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: confirm checkout-api health and error rate have recovered; decide on a path forward given v2.3.0 is quarantined.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.2%, down from 18%.\n\nI couldn't roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent production release that was healthy. It is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417, so the service rejected the request and nothing changed. I rolled back to v2.2.9 instead, the previous healthy production release.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the rollback to v2.2.9. It also notes that v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it's fixed.\n\nSomeone should look at the v2.3.0 quarantine, since it affects which version can go forward. Re-enabling v2.3.0 would need a decision from whoever owns the CVE quarantine.", "type": "text"}]}]}